settings-addons-channel-title = Update channel
settings-addons-channel-about = The newest kind of build an addon may update to. An addon can choose its own.
settings-addons-channel-hint = A channel is a floor, not a filter: allowing alpha builds still installs the newest release when that is newer. Only CurseForge and GitHub publish pre-release builds; other sources have one build, so the setting is inert there.
settings-addons-auto-title = Keep addons up to date
settings-addons-auto-about = Once per game per session, before you play.
settings-addons-auto-hint = When Lightforge starts, and again the first time you switch to another game. A launch waits for it rather than writing into the AddOns folder the client is reading. An addon can opt out on its own, and an ignored addon never moves either way.
